  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0020","idiomatic","The Tieli, the Three Fathers' House, the Southern Chancellor, Yaonian Changgun, the Nine Xishou Langjun, Yilibi, the Guoguo Xiangwen, the Ten Zhacha Langjun, the Southern Grand Prince, and the langjun—each in turn presented burial offerings, advancing saddled horses, burial garments, rhinoceros-horn and jade belts, and the like, with memorials itemizing the quantities.","The Tieli, the Three Fathers' House, the Southern Chancellor, Yaonian Changgun, the Nine Xishou Langjun, Yilibi, the Guojiu Xiangwen, the Ten Zhacha Langjun, the Southern Grand Prince, and the langjun—each in turn presented burial offerings, advancing saddled horses, burial garments, rhinoceros-horn and jade belts, and the like, with memorials itemizing the quantities.","s0020 lists 國舅詳穩 among the mourners; 國舅 is the Guojiu (imperial maternal-uncle) office, so “Guoguo Xiangwen” is a mistranslation and “Guojiu Xiangwen” is correct.","high","applied"],
    ["s0020","literal","Tieli, the Three Fathers' House, the Southern Chancellor, Yaonian Changgun, the Nine Xishou Langjun, Yilibi, Guoguo Xiangwen, the Ten Zhacha Langjun, the Southern Grand Prince, and langjun—each in order presented burial offerings, advancing saddled horses, burial garments, rhinoceros and jade belts, and the like, with memorials listing the quantities.","Tieli, the Three Fathers' House, the Southern Chancellor, Yaonian Changgun, the Nine Xishou Langjun, Yilibi, Guojiu Xiangwen, the Ten Zhacha Langjun, the Southern Grand Prince, and langjun—each in order presented burial offerings, advancing saddled horses, burial garments, rhinoceros and jade belts, and the like, with memorials listing the quantities.","s0020 lists 國舅詳穩 among the mourners; 國舅 is the Guojiu (imperial maternal-uncle) office, so “Guoguo Xiangwen” is a mistranslation and “Guojiu Xiangwen” is correct.","high","applied"]
  ],
